.TH tuodf n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuodf
.PP
Minimal OpenDocument helpers in pure Tcl: write and read text documents (\fB.odt\fR), read slides (\fB.odp\fR) and spreadsheets (\fB.ods\fR).
.PP
\fBtuodf\fR creates and reads simple paragraph\-based ODF text documents. It is not a full ODF toolkit; for rich styles, tables, images, spreadsheets, and Draw content use a dedicated ODF library.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuodf 0.2
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tuodf::createText odtFile paragraphs ?-title T? ?-creator C?
::tclutils::tuodf::text odtFile
::tclutils::tuodf::paragraphs odtFile
::tclutils::tuodf::part odtFile name
::tclutils::tuodf::parts odtFile
::tclutils::tuodf::sheets odsFile                 ;# table names, in order
::tclutils::tuodf::rows odsFile ?-sheet NAME|INDEX?  ;# one table as rows
.CE
.PP
\fBparagraphs\fR returns the text of every paragraph and heading in document order (headings since 0.2; up to 0.1 they were left out). It also finds the paragraphs inside tables and lists, in spreadsheet cells (\fB.ods\fR) and on slides (\fB.odp\fR), so \fBtext\fR works as a plain\-text extract for search.
.PP
\fBsheets\fR and \fBrows\fR read a spreadsheet (\fB.ods\fR, 0.2). \fBrows\fR gives one table (default the first; \fB\-sheet\fR takes the name or the index from 1) as a list of rows, each a list of cell texts: the paragraphs of the cell joined by \fB\en\fR, what the cell shows, not the stored value. A merged\-away cell is empty. Repeated empty cells and rows at the end of a row or table are dropped; a repeated cell or row with content counts at most 1000 times, so a crafted file cannot fill the memory. An unknown sheet is \fB{TCLUTILS TUODF SHEET name}\fR.
.PP
Numeric character references (\fB&#252;\fR, \fB&#x20AC;\fR) are decoded; up to 2026\-10\-30 only the five named entities were, and \fB&#252;\fR stayed as it was. A number past Unicode becomes U+FFFD.
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tuodf

::tclutils::tuodf::createText demo.odt \
    {{First paragraph} {Second with äöüß} {} {Fourth}} \
    -title Demo -creator Tcl

puts [::tclutils::tuodf::text demo.odt]
.CE
.SS Notes
.PP
The generated container keeps \fBmimetype\fR as the first entry and stored (uncompressed). Output uses a fixed valid timestamp for deterministic builds. All entries are currently stored, not deflated, so generated files are valid but larger than compressed ODTs.
.PP
The reader is a lightweight paragraph extractor, not a complete XML/ODF parser.
